Package: laccy
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-laccy
Description: Lightweight, keyboard-first clipboard manager for GNOME
 Laccy records text, images and files you copy, and opens a popup to search
 your history and copy an item again.
 .
 This package has the popup and preferences (laccy), the history daemon
 (laccyd) and laccy-wayland. On GNOME, also install
 gnome-shell-extension-laccy, which watches the clipboard. On Sway, Hyprland,
 Niri and other Wayland compositors that support ext-data-control-v1,
 laccy-wayland does that instead: start it with your session and bind a key
 to laccy in the compositor's config.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-laccy
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         gnome-shell (>= 50~),
         laccy (>= ${source:Version}),
         laccy (<< ${source:Version}.1~)
Description: GNOME Shell extension for the Laccy clipboard manager
 The GNOME Shell part of Laccy: it watches the clipboard, adds the top bar
 icon and the shortcut, and puts items picked in the popup back on the
 clipboard.
